WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:06.707
After dropping the jewel, Swallow felt wonderful.

2
00:00:06.708 --> 00:00:11.052
"I'm so glad I stayed to help the prince," he thought.

3
00:00:11.053 --> 00:00:17.666
"And the seamstress. Now it's time to leave for Egypt."

4
00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:21.282
Swallow began flying east.

5
00:00:21.283 --> 00:00:29.624
But he wasn't alone. A large hawk was flying right above him.

6
00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:36.166
"Oh no!" Swallow thought. "That hawk looks hungry!"

7
00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:41.000
Swoosh! Swallow switched directions and flew back to town.

8
00:00:41.001 --> 00:00:45.249
The hawk did not follow him.

9
00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:50.082
"Phew! That was scary," Swallow thought.

10
00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:53.142
He was about to begin the journey again.

11
00:00:53.143 --> 00:00:57.433
Suddenly he heard a long, deep moan.

12
00:00:57.434 --> 00:01:01.647
"That's Prince! Is he in trouble?"

13
00:01:01.648 --> 00:01:04.499
Swallow zoomed back.

14
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:11.652
The statue was crying again.

15
00:01:11.653 --> 00:01:16.291
"Prince! Why are you sad?" Swallow asked.

16
00:01:16.292 --> 00:01:20.118
"The seamstress was so grateful for the jewel.

17
00:01:20.119 --> 00:01:24.082
Now she can buy her son's medicine."

18
00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:30.707
"Thank you." The statue sniffed.

19
00:01:30.708 --> 00:01:42.527
"But there are so many more people like her. Poor, sick, and unhappy."

20
00:01:42.528 --> 00:01:51.499
Swallow sighed. "What if I help someone else? Would that make you feel better?"

21
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.376
"What about Egypt?"

22
00:01:54.377 --> 00:02:03.131
"I will go tomorrow," Swallow said. "I can't leave while you're so sad."

23
00:02:03.132 --> 00:02:07.709
The next day Swallow plucked the other ruby from the statue's belt.

24
00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:11.624
Then he flew to the docks by the river. At

25
00:02:11.625 --> 00:02:17.824
one dock a captain was talking to his crew. "Finish

26
00:02:17.825 --> 00:02:24.749
loading the ship. We set sail for Egypt today!" "That's

27
00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:28.291
where I'm going!" Swallow thought. "See

28
00:02:28.292 --> 00:02:33.582
you there! But first, my errand for the prince." Swallow

29
00:02:33.583 --> 00:02:39.832
swooped through crowds, past mothers with crying children. He

30
00:02:39.833 --> 00:02:47.582
picked up breadcrumbs and dropped them for hungry dogs. "Everyone

31
00:02:47.583 --> 00:02:50.582
needs something," he thought. "But

32
00:02:50.583 --> 00:02:53.675
I can't help everyone .

33
00:02:53.676 --> 00:02:56.811
I need to find the person I'm looking for.

34
00:02:56.812 --> 00:03:01.998
Then I'll leave for Egypt, just like that ship."

35
00:03:01.999 --> 00:03:05.749
At last, Swallow spotted her.

36
00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:10.826
He dove through the crowd and landed near a young girl.

37
00:03:10.827 --> 00:03:14.212
She wore a thin sweater and was shivering.

38
00:03:14.213 --> 00:03:19.243
In her hands she held a basket of eggs.

39
00:03:19.244 --> 00:03:25.541
"Eggs for sale! Please, buy my eggs," she called.

40
00:03:25.542 --> 00:03:33.874
A woman stopped and curled her lip. "No one will buy broken eggs!"

41
00:03:33.875 --> 00:03:41.624
"But I must sell some! Or I'll have no money to bring to the orphanage," the girl said.

42
00:03:41.625 --> 00:03:46.666
"Then we'll all go hungry!"

43
00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:51.832
The woman shrugged and walked away.

44
00:03:51.833 --> 00:03:55.624
Swallow felt a pang in his chest.

45
00:03:55.625 --> 00:03:59.832
"How unkind," he thought.

46
00:03:59.833 --> 00:04:02.756
He flew closer to the girl.

47
00:04:02.757 --> 00:04:11.266
Then he carefully dropped the jewel into her basket.

